## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to design a secure, scalable OpenAI deployment with strict per-tenant isolation, governance, and rollout strategies in Azure.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant RBAC and per-tenant KBs in Cognitive Search
- Prompt-guard layer to prevent injection and data leakage
- PII redaction with Text Analytics
- Canary rollouts behind API Management
- Auditable logs to Data Lake and RBAC alignment via Azure AD

## Code Example
```javascript
// Guard layer sketch
async function guardPrompt(input, tenantId) {
  const policy = await kb.fetchTenantPolicy(tenantId);
  if (policy.blockList.some(r => input.includes(r))) {
    throw new Error('Input blocked by policy');
  }
  // optional rewriting rules
  return input;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would policy KB updates be rolled out without affecting active tenants?
- What are latency trade-offs and how would you mitigate them at scale?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical APIM quota implementation and OpenAI routing for multi-tenant SaaS architectures.

## Key Concepts
- API Management policies with rate-limit-by-key
- Tenant-scoped routing via request headers
- Telemetry integration with Application Insights

## Code Example
```xml
<policies>
  <inbound>
    <base />
    <set-variable name='TenantID' value='@(context.Request.Headers.GetValueOrDefault("x-tenant-id","default"))' />
    <rate-limit-by-key calls='60' renewal-period='60' key='@(context.Variables["TenantID"])' />
  </inbound>
</policies>
```

```javascript
module.exports = async function (context, req) {
  const tenantId = req.headers['x-tenant-id'] || 'default';
  const startTime = Date.now();

  try {
    const response = await callOpenAI(req.body);

    // Log usage to Application Insights
    context.log('TenantUsage', {
      tenantId,
      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
      duration: Date.now() - startTime,
      status: 'success'
    });

    return { status: 200, body: response };
  } catch (error) {
    context.log.error('TenantError', { tenantId, error: error.message });
    return { status: 500, body: { error: 'Service unavailable' } };
  }
};
```

## Validation Approach
Test with multiple tenant IDs using load testing tools, verify rate limits trigger at 60 requests/minute per tenant, and confirm telemetry appears in Application Insights queries.

